The status badge for `SessionCard` is rendered in **`packages/client/src/components/session/SessionCard.tsx`**, and its color derivation logic is defined in **`packages/client/src/lib/session/session-status-visuals.ts`**.

---

### 1. Where it is rendered

In **`packages/client/src/components/session/SessionCard.tsx`**:

* **Status Icon & Badge (Desktop)**: Around lines **843–855** in the card's Line 1 header:
  ```tsx
  <span
    className={`relative inline-flex flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-[var(--bg-tertiary)] shadow-sm ${iconStatusColor}`}
    data-testid="session-status-icon"
    data-status-shape={statusShape}
    title={`${sourceLabels[session.source] ?? session.source} — ${session.status}`}
  >
    <Icon path={sourceIcons[session.source] ?? mdiConsoleLine} size={0.45} />
    <StatusShapeBadge shape={statusShape} colorClass={iconStatusColor} />
  </span>
  ```
* **Status Icon & Badge (Mobile)**: Around lines **683–692** in the mobile layout.
* **`<StatusShapeBadge>` Component**: Lines **114–128** in `SessionCard.tsx`, which overlays the WCAG non-hue geometry shape marker (`data-testid="session-status-shape"`) styled with `colorClass={iconStatusColor}`.
* *(Companion text)*: **`<StatusText>`** at lines **78–109** renders the inline status text (e.g., "Thinking…", "Needs you", current tool, or "Idle").

---

### 2. How its color is chosen

The color is derived via two functions in **`packages/client/src/lib/session/session-status-visuals.ts`**:

1. **`deriveDotColorWithFlags(session, { hasError, isRetrying, hasWidgetBarPrompt, hasNotice })`** (lines **95–111**):
   Evaluates session state in strict precedence (highest to lowest):
   * `hasError` &rarr; `"bg-[var(--status-error)]"`
   * `isChatRoutedAskUser(...)` (`currentTool === "ask_user"` not handled by widget bar) &rarr; `"bg-[var(--status-needs-you)]"`
   * `session.resuming` or `isRetrying` &rarr; `"bg-[var(--status-working)] animate-pulse"`
   * `hasNotice` &rarr; `"bg-[var(--status-notice)]"`
   * `statusColors[session.status]` (lines **31–36**):
     * `"streaming"` &rarr; `"bg-[var(--status-working)] animate-pulse"`
     * `"active"` / `"idle"` &rarr; `"bg-[var(--status-idle)]"`
     * `"ended"` &rarr; `"bg-[var(--bg-surface)]"`

2. **`deriveIconStatusColor(dotColor, session.status)`** (lines **122–134**):
   Converts the background token into the text-color class applied to the badge:
   * If `status === "ended"` and `dotColor` is the default surface token &rarr; `"text-[var(--text-muted)]"`
   * Otherwise &rarr; replaces the leading `bg-` with `text-` (e.g., `text-[var(--status-working)]`, `text-[var(--status-needs-you)]`, `text-[var(--status-idle)]`).
